From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcrypt: Refuse unknown symmetric BCryptDecrypt flags.

BCryptDecrypt with a symmetric key fails with STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER for
flags other than BCRYPT_BLOCK_PADDING ("can be zero or the following value"),
as BCryptEncrypt already does (patch 1693); it returned STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.

Gate: test/bcrypt-decryptflags-gate.sh (64/32).
---
 dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c b/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c
index bb6de88..1571d57 100644
--- a/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c
+++ b/dlls/bcrypt/bcrypt_main.c
@@ -2295,8 +2295,13 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI BCryptDecrypt( BCRYPT_KEY_HANDLE handle, UCHAR *input, ULONG inp
     {
         if (flags & ~BCRYPT_BLOCK_PADDING)
         {
-            FIXME( "flags %#lx not supported\n", flags );
+            /* only block padding applies to a symmetric key, as in BCryptEncrypt */
+            WARN( "invalid flags %#lx\n", flags );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DECRYPT_FLAGS_NOTIMPL
+            return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+#else
             return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+#endif
         }
 
         EnterCriticalSection( &key->u.s.cs );
